# Adaptation Engine v2 — Evidence Stream & Rate Policy Specification
# SSi Learning App
#
# Version: 0.6.0 (WP-0..WP-8 + VAD phase 1: SimplePlayer timing wiring + cycle_prosody)
# Last updated: 2026-07-28
#
# 2026-07-28 (VAD feedback phase 1, founder-ruled):
# - GROUND-TRUTH CORRECTION to "Producer #1 LIVE" below: the latency producer's
#   INPUT was dead on the live path until today. startTimingCycle /
#   markPhaseTransition / endTimingCycle were only driven by the legacy
#   handleCycleEvent path (CycleOrchestrator), which SimplePlayer never routes
#   through — so lastTimingResult stayed null, recordCycle's latency guard never
#   passed, and no latency (or envelope) evidence was ever produced in real
#   sessions, even for VAD-consented learners. Fixed: simplePlayer.onPhaseChanged
#   now drives the analyzer lifecycle (start at 'prompt' for speaking cycles —
#   pauseDuration > 0 + legoId; PROMPT_END/PAUSE/VOICE_1/VOICE_2 marks; a window
#   left open by a skip is reset at next prompt, never mis-attributed), and
#   onCycleCompleted closes the window and captures the result.
# - NEW telemetry event `cycle_prosody` (one per voiced speaking cycle, VAD
#   consent only) into player_events via usePlayerLog: the append-only
#   longitudinal row (learner, cycle/lego/seed identity, target1 audioId,
#   response_latency_ms, learner_duration_ms, duration_delta_ms, quality flags,
#   learner-side EnvelopeMetadata block, extractorVersion, playbackSpeed).
#   The learner envelope is computed UNCONDITIONALLY by the VAD (stage2_enabled
#   gates only the adaptation consumer), so the corpus is envelope-complete from
#   day one; audioId joins to course_audio_envelope, making the prosody-match
#   measure computable retroactively once WP-7b populates that table. Rows are
#   retention-exempt by founder ruling (docs/vad-feedback-design.md §5).
# - SCHEMA STEER (founder, mid-build 2026-07-28): the event logs INTERMEDIATE
#   features, not just derived scalars — EnvelopeMetadata now carries an
#   optional `contour` (smoothed linear envelope, peak-normalized 0-100 ints,
#   ≤ CONTOUR_MAX_POINTS=128, bucket-averaged beyond; `contourGridMs` is the
#   effective timebase) so future prosody metrics (DTW-style similarity,
#   phrase-matched CEFR variance bands) recompute over historical rows.
#   Additive output only: extraction constants and all existing derived
#   numbers unchanged, extractor version stays 1. The event also carries
#   speech_start/end, overlap flags, and peak/average energy dB. WP-7b note:
#   when the dashboard-repo envelope job runs, it should store the MODEL-side
#   contour too, or contour-vs-contour similarity has no model operand.
# Grounded in: docs/adaptation/adaptation-v2-build-spec.md §2/§3/§4/§5.1/§5.2/§5.3/§6
#              (design authority; packages/player-vue/public/docs/metrics-vision.html
#              wins on conflict)
#
# Core Insight: All evidence about the learner — today's behavioural taps and
# skips, tomorrow's voice-envelope numbers — flows through ONE narrow typed
# wire. The scheduler (rate policy, workstream C2) never branches on which
# producer emitted an observation; it only ever reads merged per-unit series.
# That property — a second producer plugs in with zero scheduler changes — is
# this module's acceptance test (see evidence.test.ts, "acceptance test" suite).
#
# Implementation Status (verified 2026-07-14):
# - MasteryEvidence / EvidenceSink / EvidenceAggregator: LIVE (WP-0)
#   packages/core/src/learning/evidence.ts
# - Producer #1 (latency, via useAdaptationEngine.recordCycle): LIVE (WP-3)
#   emits alongside the untouched v1 MetricsTracker flow, into the ONE
#   shared aggregator (see player_wiring module below)
# - Producer #2 (behavioural taps/skips): LIVE (WP-1), now sharing the SAME
#   aggregator as producer #1 (WP-3 folded it in — see player_wiring)
#   packages/player-vue/src/composables/useBehaviouralEvidence.ts — hooked
#   beside every logEvent call site in LearningPlayer.vue
# - Client envelope extractor: LIVE (WP-6)
#   packages/core/src/audio/envelopeMetadata.ts + VoiceActivityDetector.ts
#   (SpeechTimingResult.envelope) — pure, tested against synthetic n-peak
#   envelopes; raw samples never leave VoiceActivityDetector
# - Model envelope schema + client batch fetch/cache: LIVE (WP-7a)
#   supabase/migrations/20260714_course_audio_envelope.sql (GATED — for Tom
#   to apply, not yet live) + packages/player-vue/src/composables/
#   useEnvelopeMetadataCache.ts. Dashboard-repo pipeline job (WP-7b) is a
#   separate brief in ssi-dashboard-v7-clean.
# - Producer #3 (envelope metadata, WP-8): LIVE, STILL UNWIRED
#   packages/player-vue/src/composables/useEnvelopeEvidence.ts — pure delta
#   math + EvidenceSink emission, fully tested; the shared aggregator this
#   module needs now exists (WP-3), but registering recordEnvelopeEvidence
#   in the cycle-complete path is deliberately left for the stage-2 track
#   (parallel, separately gated by stage2_enabled) — not part of WP-3's scope
# - Rate policy (RatePolicyEngine): LIVE (WP-2), wired to the player (WP-3)
#   packages/core/src/learning/ratePolicy.ts
# - Player wiring (RoundPlan applied via shouldSkipCycle overrides +
#   breather-round assembly): LIVE (WP-3, this spec's new player_wiring module)
# - Persistence (snapshot/hydrate wired to learner_lego_metrics): LIVE (WP-4,
#   lite scope) — evidence_series JSONB column, gated migration
#   supabase/migrations/20260714_lego_metrics_evidence_series.sql
# - Safety rails (kill switch, shadow-mode logging): LIVE (WP-5, folded into
#   WP-3's player wiring) — algorithm_config.adaptation_v2, adaptation_plan
#   shadow log event. The ?adaptdebug=1 dev overlay (§6.5(c)) is NOT built —
#   not required for the shadow-mode deliverable, earn it when a human needs
#   to eyeball live lever positions during soak.
# - Boundary sensing (WP-9, inter-peak gap analysis): NOT BUILT — out of scope
#   for WP-6/7a/8, a separate, deliberately timeboxed work package

module: evidence_stream
  purpose: >
    Define the one wire all mastery evidence travels on, and the per-unit
    merge that turns however many producers into one time-ordered difficulty
    series per unit — the exact shape computeLocalDifficulty/computeCurvature
    already consume.

  input_convention: >
    Higher `value` = more difficulty/struggle — the same convention as
    localDifficulty.ts's UnitSeries. Producers normalise into a common
    ~[0..3] band (per-producer mapping lives in each producer's own spec,
    e.g. the WP-1 behavioural mapping table) so series from different sources
    mix sanely once merged for one unit.

  data:
    EvidenceSource: enum [ latency, behaviour, envelope ]
    MasteryEvidence:
      unitId: string            # LEGO id (canonical); boundary key later (boundary:{legoId}:{gapIndex})
      unitKind: enum [ lego, boundary ]
      source: EvidenceSource
      value: number             # difficulty-bearing, higher = more struggle
      weight: number             # producer confidence, [0..1]
      cycleId: string?           # ties same-cycle evidence together for the collapse rule
      occurredAtMs: number       # performance.now() epoch of the session — the series' time axis
    EvidenceSeries:
      values: number[]           # time-ordered, merged
      x: number[]                # matching time axis (occurredAtMs of each collapsed sample)

  api:
    EvidenceSink.record(evidence: MasteryEvidence) -> void:
      >  The only way any producer writes evidence. Implemented by
         EvidenceAggregator; producers hold only this narrow interface, never
         the concrete aggregator — that narrowness is what makes producers
         interchangeable.
    createEvidenceAggregator() -> EvidenceAggregator:
      >  Construct a fresh, empty aggregator (one per learner session).
    EvidenceAggregator.getSeries(unitId) -> EvidenceSeries:
      >  Time-ordered merged difficulty series for one unit, ready to hand to
         assessLocalDifficulty/computeCurvature.
    EvidenceAggregator.readyUnits(minSamples) -> string[]:
      >  Units with >= minSamples merged samples — the per-round policy sweep
         set (workstream C2 / ratePolicy.ts, WP-2).
    EvidenceAggregator.snapshot() -> Map<unitId, EvidenceSeries>:
      >  Defensive-copy snapshot for persistence (WP-4: learner_lego_metrics
         evidence_series column).
    EvidenceAggregator.hydrate(data: Map<unitId, EvidenceSeries>) -> void:
      >  Seed an aggregator from a prior snapshot (session resume). Hydrated
         samples have no recoverable cycleId, so they never collapse with each
         other or with new evidence — only fresh same-cycle observations do.

  merge_rule: >
    Evidence landing within the SAME cycle for the SAME unit (same cycleId)
    collapses into one sample: value = Σ(vᵢ·wᵢ)/Σwᵢ, and the sample's x moves
    to the latest occurredAtMs in that cycle. Evidence with no cycleId, or a
    different cycleId than the unit's most recent sample, always appends as a
    new sample in time order. This keeps one merged series per unit regardless
    of how many producers fire in a given cycle — exactly what
    computeLocalDifficulty wants, and exactly what lets a second producer plug
    in without the aggregator or its consumers changing shape.

  ring_buffer: >
    Each unit's series is capped at EVIDENCE_SERIES_RING_CAP (20) collapsed
    samples — the same cap as the existing recent_latency_samples column on
    learner_lego_metrics. Oldest samples are dropped first (FIFO).

  guarantees:
    - producer_agnostic: the aggregator and its consumers never branch on `source`
    - pure: no Vue/Supabase coupling; no app/storage side effects
    - non_mutating_snapshot: mutating a snapshot's contents never affects the aggregator
    - hydrate_is_seed_only: hydrated samples do not retroactively collapse with each other

  tests:
    - packages/core/src/learning/evidence.test.ts   # merge weighting (2-way and 3-way),
                                                     #   ring cap + FIFO drop, per-cycle collapse,
                                                     #   no-cycleId no-collapse, multi-unit isolation,
                                                     #   readyUnits threshold, snapshot/hydrate round-trip,
                                                     #   defensive-copy snapshot, and the acceptance test:
                                                     #   two distinct `source`s merge into one series the
                                                     #   scheduler reads uniformly with zero branching.

module: behavioural_producer
  purpose: >
    Producer #2 on the evidence wire (build spec §3). Maps the behavioural
    events already logged today (phase_skip, tap_skip, lego_skip, tap_pause/
    tap_play, turbo_toggle, belt_skip, audio_retry) into MasteryEvidence at
    the logEvent emit site in LearningPlayer.vue — no round-trip through
    player_events; the DB copy stays the analytics record. Mic-free: guest /
    VAD-unavailable learners still produce this evidence, which is what makes
    stage 1 work without a microphone.

  mapping_table: >
    All values PROPOSED (build spec §3), tuned into the same ~[0..3]
    struggle band as normalised latency:
      phase_skip forward, elapsed < 40% of pauseDuration -> value 0.3, weight 0.6 (confident)
      phase_skip forward, elapsed >= 40% of pauseDuration -> value 0.6, weight 0.4 (mild confidence)
      phase_skip back or replay                           -> value 1.8, weight 0.8 (uncertainty)
      tap_skip during='cycle' (whole-cycle skip)           -> value 1.2, weight 0.3 (ambiguous avoidance/boredom)
      tap_skip during anything else (intro/pod_lap/...)    -> dropped, not learner evidence
      lego_skip back                                       -> value 2.0, weight 0.8 (struggle with the round's LEGO)
      lego_skip forward                                    -> value 0.4, weight 0.5 ("got this / too easy")
      tap_pause mid-PAUSE-phase, followed by tap_play       -> value 1.4, weight 0.5 (processing time needed)
      tap_pause outside the PAUSE phase                    -> dropped (not learner struggle)
      turbo_toggle, belt_skip                               -> dropped from unit series; set manualOverrideActive
      audio_retry                                           -> dropped (infrastructure, not learner evidence)

  manual_dial_rule: >
    turbo_toggle and belt_skip are the learner outranking the engine (paper
    Principle 1) — they never enter a unit's difficulty series. Instead they
    set a session-level manualOverrideActive flag the rate policy reads to
    widen its hysteresis dead-zone (build spec §4.5), so the engine yields to
    the learner's own judgement rather than fighting it.

  tap_pause_correlation: >
    A tap_pause is only candidate evidence when it lands during the PAUSE
    phase (Phase.SPEAK) — pausing during intro/welcome/pod-lap/commentary
    isn't learner struggle. The producer holds that one pending pause
    (keyed on unitId + cycleId) until the next tap_play, at which point it
    emits the "processing time needed" reading; a second tap_pause (or one
    outside the PAUSE phase) overwrites/clears the pending state without
    emitting, and a tap_play with no matching pending pause is a no-op.

  api:
    useBehaviouralEvidence(sink: EvidenceSink, nowMs?) -> UseBehaviouralEvidenceReturn:
      >  Holds only the EvidenceSink interface (never the concrete
         aggregator) — the composable doesn't know or care where its
         evidence ends up.
    UseBehaviouralEvidenceReturn.onPlayerEvent(type, payload, currentCycle?) -> void:
      >  Called with one line added beside each existing logEvent(type,
         payload) call site, usually reusing the same payload object.
         unitId resolves from currentCycle.legoId, falling back to
         payload.legoId / payload.fromLegoId.
    UseBehaviouralEvidenceReturn.isManualOverrideActive() -> boolean:
      >  True once a manual-dial event has fired this session (build spec §4.3).

  wired_at: >
    packages/player-vue/src/components/LearningPlayer.vue — one
    useBehaviouralEvidence(createEvidenceAggregator()) instance constructed
    alongside the existing adaptationEngine ref; onPlayerEvent hooked beside
    logEvent at every phase_skip / tap_skip / lego_skip / tap_pause / tap_play
    / turbo_toggle / belt_skip call site. audio_retry is left unhooked — the
    mapping drops it unconditionally, so there is nothing for a hook to do.

  guarantees:
    - emit_site_only: no round-trip through player_events; evidence derives
      from the same in-memory event payload logEvent receives
    - pure_classification: the value/weight mapping for every event type is a
      pure function (classifyPhaseSkip / classifyTapSkip / classifyLegoSkip),
      independently testable against the mapping table above
    - manual_dial_never_in_series: turbo_toggle/belt_skip never call sink.record()
    - guest_safe: no VAD/mic dependency anywhere in this producer

  tests:
    - packages/player-vue/src/composables/useBehaviouralEvidence.test.ts
      # pure classifiers against every mapping-table row; full onPlayerEvent
      # integration per event type incl. dropped-during branches; tap_pause/
      # tap_play correlation (mid-PAUSE match, wrong-phase no-op, wrong-LEGO
      # no-op, superseding a stale pending pause, orphan tap_play); dropped
      # event types (audio_retry) never emit; manual-dial events never enter
      # a series but do set the override flag; unrecognised event types and
      # unresolvable unitId are silently ignored.

module: rate_policy
  purpose: >
    Decide, at each round boundary, how to spend the session's finite
    practice budget across CONSOLIDATE / DEFER / DRILL (build spec §4; the
    paper §03). The single consumer of EvidenceAggregator series (via B4's
    assessLocalDifficulty) and introduction-order criticality. Pure — decides
    only; WP-3 (player wiring, not yet built) is the only thing that ever
    applies a RoundPlan.

  binding_pedagogy: >
    Owner decision, do not invert: default lean is consolidate + defer; drill
    is reserved for the structurally critical few, where criticality =
    introduction order (earliest `criticalFrontloadFraction` of the course's
    LEGO ordinals), NEVER corpus frequency. Enforced STRUCTURALLY, not just by
    default numbers: a critical unit's confirmed struggle has no code path to
    the round-level buildCount/consolidateCount/spacedRepCap decision at all —
    it can only nudge that unit's own pause multiplier. Separately, no
    struggle signal of any kind has a code path that RAISES buildCount or
    spacedRepCap above their scripted defaults — the only way those levers
    rise back up is quiet-round decay toward the default, never a struggle
    event. "Drill" therefore always means "hold at scripted + pause + the
    existing N-1 spaced-rep 3x multiplier" — no new drilling machinery exists
    or is built.

  data:
    LeverBounds: { floor: number, ceiling: number, scripted: number, step: number }
    RatePolicyBounds:
      buildCount: LeverBounds        # PROPOSED floor 3 / ceiling 7 / scripted 7 / step 1
      consolidateCount: LeverBounds  # PROPOSED floor 1 / ceiling 4 / scripted 2 / step 1
      spacedRepCap: LeverBounds      # PROPOSED floor 6 / ceiling 12 / scripted 12 / step 1
      pauseMultiplier: LeverBounds   # PROPOSED floor 0.7 / ceiling 1.4 / step 0.05
      breatherMinRoundGap: number    # PROPOSED 3 ("at most 1 breather per 3 rounds")
    RatePolicyConfig:
      bounds: RatePolicyBounds
      criticalFrontloadFraction: number    # PROPOSED 0.15
      hysteresisReads: number              # PROPOSED 2 consecutive confirming reads
      decayRounds: number                  # PROPOSED 5 quiet rounds to fully decay a one-step nudge
      manualOverrideDeadZoneMultiplier: number  # PROPOSED 2 — widens hysteresisReads while the learner
                                                 #   has exercised belt_skip/turbo_toggle this session
    RoundBoundaryInput:
      roundLegoId: string                  # the round about to play's own LEGO
      roundLegoOrdinal: number             # its introduction ordinal (criticality guard)
      courseLegoCount: number              # criticality-fraction denominator
      difficulty: LocalDifficulty[]        # this boundary's B4 reads, one per ready unit
      unitOrdinals: Record<string, number> # introduction ordinal per unit id
      manualOverrideActive: boolean
      basePauseMultiplier: (legoId) => number   # the existing MasteryStateMachine ladder value,
                                                 #   BEFORE this policy's curvature nudge
    RoundPlan:
      buildCount: number
      consolidateCount: number
      spacedRepCap: number
      insertBreather: boolean              # insert a no-new-LEGO breather before the NEXT debut
      pauseMultiplier: (legoId) => number  # ladder base + curvature nudge, clamped

  api:
    createRatePolicyEngine(config?) -> RatePolicyEngine:
      >  Construct one engine per learner session (mirrors createEvidenceAggregator /
         MasteryStateMachine — the stateful-engine-over-pure-primitives pattern).
    RatePolicyEngine.planRound(input: RoundBoundaryInput) -> RoundPlan:
      >  The only mutating entry point. Advances internal hysteresis/decay state
         by exactly one round boundary and returns the plan for the round about
         to play. Never applies anything — WP-3's job.

  budget_logic: >
    Per confirmed-struggling unit (build spec §4.3), in priority order:
      1. CRITICALITY GUARD — critical unit (ordinal <= ceil(courseLegoCount *
         criticalFrontloadFraction)): round-level levers untouched; only its
         own pause multiplier nudges up. "Never defer" (paper §04).
      2. OWN-LEGO STRUGGLE — the round's own (new) LEGO is the non-critical
         struggling unit: buildCount HOLDS at scripted (new material is never
         starved of its own practice); consolidateCount rises one step; a
         breather is scheduled before the NEXT debut (slows the wholesale
         rate between rounds, never guts the current debut).
      3. DEFER (default) — some OTHER non-critical unit is struggling:
         buildCount and spacedRepCap each trim one step toward floor;
         consolidateCount rises one step — the freed budget spent on
         strengths (paper §03's "consolidate" move).
    Quiet rounds (no confirming signal) decay every off-default lever back
    toward its scripted value, `step / decayRounds` per round — "the engine's
    resting state is do nothing" (§4.5).

  hysteresis_and_bounds: >
    A lever moves only after `hysteresisReads` (default 2) CONSECUTIVE
    confirming round-boundary reads for the same unit (a steady/warming_up
    read in between resets the count) — never more than one step per
    boundary. `manualOverrideActive` multiplies the requirement by
    `manualOverrideDeadZoneMultiplier` (default 2x) for the rest of the
    session, per the paper's Principle 1 (the learner's own manual dial
    outranks the engine). Every output is clamped to RatePolicyBounds —
    enforced twice (offset-level and final-value-level) so bounds cannot be
    exceeded by any input sequence, tested adversarially.

  guarantees:
    - pure: no Vue/Supabase/player coupling; consumes LocalDifficulty reads only
    - structural_lean: no code path exists from "critical unit struggling" to a
      round-level lever move, and no code path exists that raises buildCount/
      spacedRepCap above scripted default on any struggle signal — see
      binding_pedagogy above
    - bounded: every lever clamped to its floor/ceiling on every read, under
      adversarial sustained-struggle input
    - one_step_per_boundary: no lever moves more than its configured `step`
      per `planRound` call
    - invisible: levers decay fully to scripted defaults after `decayRounds`
      of quiet, so a killed/disabled session leaves no residual state a
      learner could feel on re-enable

  tests:
    - packages/core/src/learning/ratePolicy.test.ts   # bounds unbreakable under 200-round adversarial
                                                       #   struggle; criticality guard (critical unit never
                                                       #   deferred, contrasted against a non-critical unit
                                                       #   past the cutoff); the consolidate/defer lean
                                                       #   (own-LEGO-holds vs other-unit-defers, breather
                                                       #   cadence, "no struggle ever raises a lever" proof);
                                                       #   2-read hysteresis + manual-override doubling;
                                                       #   decay-to-default over quiet rounds; golden scenario
                                                       #   traces replaying real struggling/steady/easing
                                                       #   syntheticSeries through the real assessLocalDifficulty
                                                       #   sensor (not a stub); config overrides honoured.

module: player_wiring
  purpose: >
    WP-3: wires the evidence stream (WP-0/1) and rate policy (WP-2) into the
    live player, entirely through SimplePlayer's EXISTING runtime-overrides
    surface (`shouldSkipCycle`, `getPauseDuration`) — no script regeneration,
    same mechanism Turbo already proves out. SHADOW MODE IS THE DELIVERABLE:
    the engine computes and logs a RoundPlan every round boundary, but the
    kill switch / shadow flag (WP-5, folded in here) means nothing is
    APPLIED until Tom flips `adaptation_v2.shadow` to false in the DB.

  shared_aggregator: >
    LearningPlayer.vue constructs ONE `sharedEvidenceAggregator` (module
    scope) and passes it into BOTH `useAdaptationEngine({..., aggregator:
    sharedEvidenceAggregator})` and `useBehaviouralEvidence(
    sharedEvidenceAggregator)` — the two producers now merge into one
    per-LEGO series, satisfying WP-0's acceptance test in the actual running
    player (previously each composable held its own aggregator). Latency
    evidence is emitted unconditionally inside `useAdaptationEngine.
    recordCycle` (cheap, keeps the series warm for whenever v2 is enabled) —
    the kill switch gates PLANNING/LOGGING/APPLICATION at the LearningPlayer
    level, not evidence recording.

  round_plan_computation: >
    `useAdaptationEngine.planRound(input: PlanRoundInput) -> { plan,
    difficulty }` wraps `EvidenceAggregator.readyUnits` +
    `assessLocalDifficulty` (B4) per ready unit, then
    `RatePolicyEngine.planRound`. Only the round's own (about-to-play) LEGO
    has a known introduction ordinal — `unitOrdinals` for every other unit is
    left absent, which the criticality guard treats as "never critical" (the
    policy's documented safe default) rather than guessing. `roundLegoOrdinal`
    is approximated as the LEGO's SEED NUMBER (via getSeedFromLegoId) since
    one new LEGO per round means round order tracks introduction order
    closely and criticality only needs the FRACTION through the course right,
    not an exact count; `courseLegoCount` is approximated the same way via
    `beltProgress.courseSeedCount`. Both approximations are PROPOSED — earn a
    finer ordinal map only if shadow-log data shows mis-deferring.

  application: >
    `handleRoundBoundary` computes the plan for the round about to start
    (`nextRound`) EVERY boundary the engine is enabled, logs it unconditionally,
    then applies it ONLY when `shadow:false`:
      - `computeAdaptOmitCycleIds(round, plan)` (packages/player-vue/src/
        playback/adaptationOverrides.ts) mirrors the `turboOmit` cull exactly
        — walks the round's cycles counting BUILD/USE/spaced_rep occurrences
        in order, marking the (N+1)-th-and-later of each type past
        buildCount/consolidateCount/spacedRepCap. This is a COMPLETE and
        correct realisation for buildCount/spacedRepCap (their ceiling always
        equals their scripted default in RatePolicyBounds — they can only
        ever be trimmed). consolidateCount's ceiling exceeds its scripted
        default; a RAISE there is realised via insertBreather instead (a cull
        can only trim, never invent cycles).
      - `assembleBreatherRound(loadedRounds, completedRoundIndex, nextRound,
        getPauseMultiplier)` builds a no-new-LEGO round from USE cycles
        already sitting in already-loaded rounds, whose LEGO reads
        confident/mastered on the existing pause ladder (>= 0.85 ceiling on
        `getPauseMultiplier`) — one per LEGO, oldest-loaded first, capped at
        12 cycles. Inserted via `SimplePlayer.appendRounds` (an existing,
        audited primitive — this is the SAME insertion path infinite-play
        revival batches use) at a fractional `roundNumber` (anchor - 0.5) so
        it sorts immediately before the next debut. Returns null (no
        insertion) when nothing is mastered yet.
      - `currentRoundPlan` (for the pause-multiplier nudge) and
        `adaptOmitCycleIds` (for the cull) are set ONLY on the apply branch;
        the shadow/disabled branch resets both to empty, so
        `shouldSkipCycle`/`getPauseDuration` transparently fall through to
        the pre-v2 behaviour with zero learner-visible change.

  safety_rails: >
    `algorithm_config.adaptation_v2` (useAlgorithmConfig.ts,
    `AdaptationV2Config`): `{ enabled, shadow, stage2_enabled, bounds,
    weights }`. Default (row absent, or fields missing) is `enabled:true,
    shadow:true` — "compute and log every boundary, never apply" — satisfying
    "ship with the DB flag absent -> shadow-only" via the SAME missing-row
    fallback merge pattern every other algorithm_config key already uses.
    `enabled:false` is the harder kill switch: `handleRoundBoundary` skips the
    entire adaptation-v2 block — no evidence read, no curvature computed, no
    adaptation_plan log line ("disables even shadow computation", verbatim).
    `bounds` flows into `RatePolicyEngine` via `ratePolicyConfig.bounds` at
    `useAdaptationEngine` construction, so Tom can tune floors/ceilings/steps
    without a deploy.

  shadow_log_shape: >
    One `adaptation_plan` player_event per round boundary (when enabled):
      { roundNumber, legoId,
        plan: { buildCount, consolidateCount, spacedRepCap, insertBreather },
        difficultyStates: [{ unitId, state, accelerationZ, samples }, ...],
        applied: boolean }   # true only when shadow:false
    `applied` lets a shadow-soak query separate "what the engine computed"
    from "what it would have changed" without a second event type.

  persistence: >
    WP-4 (lite scope): `LegoMetricsStore.upsertEvidenceSeries` (new, isolated
    upsert — same pattern as the existing `upsertSeries` B4 write) persists
    `EvidenceAggregator.getSeries(legoId)` per dirty LEGO on every flush;
    `initialize()` hydrates the aggregator from `learner_lego_metrics.
    evidence_series` on mount, alongside (not replacing) the existing
    `recent_latency_samples` hydrate. Gated migration (Tom applies):
    supabase/migrations/20260714_lego_metrics_evidence_series.sql — additive,
    same isolation reasoning as the 20260613 latency-series migration: a
    missing column degrades this ONE upsert in isolation, never mastery or
    the B4 series write.

  guarantees:
    - zero_learner_visible_change_in_shadow: currentRoundPlan/adaptOmitCycleIds
      are empty/null on every path except enabled&&!shadow — existing test
      suites (SimplePlayer, LearningPlayer-adjacent) pass unmodified
    - kill_switch_is_a_hard_stop: enabled:false short-circuits before any
      evidence read/curvature computation/log line, not just before applying
    - no_script_regeneration: every lever is realised through SimplePlayer's
      existing overrides surface (shouldSkipCycle, getPauseDuration) or its
      existing appendRounds primitive — no Round/Cycle mutation of the
      original generated script
    - structural_bound_reuse: buildCount/spacedRepCap realisation is provably
      complete because their ceiling equals their scripted default in
      RatePolicyBounds (ratePolicy.ts) — cull-only can never under-realise them

  tests:
    - packages/player-vue/src/playback/adaptationOverrides.test.ts   # cull
      #   matches scripted defaults (no-op); trims BUILD/USE/spaced_rep past
      #   each cap; never touches other cycle types; breather returns null
      #   pre-mastery; pulls one USE cycle per mastered LEGO; fractional
      #   roundNumber sorts before the anchor; distinct legoId; caps at 12 +
      #   dedupes; only considers rounds up to the given index (inclusive)
    - packages/core/src/persistence/LegoMetricsStore.test.ts   # evidence_series
      #   load/default-when-absent; upsertEvidenceSeries payload shape +
      #   no-op-on-empty, isolated from mastery columns
    - existing suites (packages/core, packages/player-vue) pass unmodified —
      the shadow-mode zero-visible-change assertion

module: envelope_extractor
  purpose: >
    Stage-2 client-side extractor (build spec §5.1, WP-6). Turns the VAD's
    own timestamped RMS-dB samples — already collected every rAF frame,
    previously discarded to peak/mean only — into five derived numbers, on
    EXACTLY the algorithm/constants pinned for comparability with the
    dashboard-repo's offline model-voice extractor (WP-7b). No second
    AnalyserNode, no new audio path, no recording. Raw samples are consumed
    and discarded inside VoiceActivityDetector; only EnvelopeMetadata ever
    leaves it (the privacy invariant, build spec §6.6).

  constants: >
    packages/core/src/audio/envelope-extractor-v1.json — copied VERBATIM from
    ssi-dashboard-v7-clean/services/shared/envelope-extractor-v1.json (both
    repos read the same file rather than re-deriving numbers, so client and
    pipeline can't drift): version 1, gridMs 20, smoothingTaps 3 (60ms window),
    peakProminenceRatio 0.25, peakMinSeparationMs 120, minSampleCount 10.

  data:
    TimedEnergySample: { t: number, db: number }   # performance.now()-relative ms, VAD's getCurrentEnergy() dB
    EnvelopeMetadata:
      durationMs: number         # learner_duration_ms, carried through from the VAD's own speech timing
      peakCount: number          # syllable-scale energy peaks
      peakToMeanRatio: number    # max linear RMS / mean linear RMS over the speech region
      meanPeakWidthMs: number    # mean full-width-at-half-prominence
      sampleCount: number        # grid points after resampling — the capture-quality guard
      weight: number             # 0 = discard the cycle (sampleCount < minSampleCount)

  algorithm: >
    1. Sort timestamped samples, resample onto the fixed 20ms grid via LINEAR
       INTERPOLATION over {t,db} pairs (dB->linear en route) — the one
       deliberate divergence from the server, which windows already-uniform
       fixed-rate PCM; this is what makes the client robust to rAF's
       display-locked, throttle-prone cadence (cadence-independence, tested
       against both jittered timestamps and a sparser/throttled sample rate).
    2. 3-tap (60ms) centered moving average — syllable-scale smoothing.
    3. peakToMeanRatio = max/mean over the smoothed grid.
    4. Peaks: scipy peak_prominences definition (extend outward from a local
       maximum to the array boundary or a higher sample, prominence = height
       - max(leftMin, rightMin)); accept prominence >= 25% of (max-mean);
       greedy accept in descending-height order enforcing >= 120ms minimum
       separation between accepted peaks.
    5. Width per accepted peak = span (in ms) where the grid stays >=
       (peak height - prominence/2); meanPeakWidthMs = mean across peaks.
    6. sampleCount < minSampleCount (10, ~1/5 second) -> weight 0, all other
       fields zeroed — the capture-quality gate.
    Flat/silent captures (no dynamic range: max <= mean) short-circuit to zero
    peaks rather than treating float noise as syllables.

  api:
    extractEnvelopeMetadata(samples: TimedEnergySample[], durationMs: number,
                             constants?) -> EnvelopeMetadata:
      >  Pure function. Never mutates or retains `samples` — verified by a
         raw-array-containment test asserting the input array is unchanged
         and the result object carries only the 6 scalar fields.

  wired_at: >
    packages/core/src/audio/VoiceActivityDetector.ts — continuousAnalyzeLoop
    now also pushes {t: performance.now(), db: energy} onto a private
    continuousEnergyTimeline (continuous mode ONLY; legacy analyzeLoop /
    energySamples untouched). stopContinuousMonitoring filters the timeline
    to the confirmed speech window [speechStartMs, speechEndMs], calls
    extractEnvelopeMetadata once, attaches the result as
    SpeechTimingResult.envelope, then immediately clears
    continuousEnergyTimeline — the raw array never survives past this call.
    envelope is left undefined when no speech was detected.

  guarantees:
    - pure: no Vue/Supabase coupling
    - raw_array_containment: samples never returned, never retained past the
      one stopContinuousMonitoring call that consumes them
    - cadence_independent: peak count is stable under both timestamp jitter
      and a coarser (throttled) sampling interval, for the same underlying
      envelope shape
    - server_comparable: same constants file, same grid/smoothing/prominence/
      width algorithm as the dashboard-repo's offline extractor (WP-7b) —
      verified by that repo's own golden-file test (same clip -> same
      numbers within tolerance), not duplicated here

  tests:
    - packages/core/src/audio/envelopeMetadata.test.ts   # n-peak synthetic
      #   fixtures (3-gaussian-bump -> peakCount 3); jittered-timestamp and
      #   throttled-sample-rate cadence-independence; flat/silent -> 0 peaks;
      #   close-peak merging under the 120ms separation floor; mumbled
      #   (wide-sigma) vs crisp (narrow-sigma) -> wider meanPeakWidthMs;
      #   sub-minSampleCount -> weight 0; empty-array and out-of-order-
      #   timestamp edge cases; raw-array containment.
    - packages/core/src/audio/VoiceActivityDetector.test.ts   # continuous-mode
      #   envelope wiring: attaches EnvelopeMetadata when speech was detected
      #   (manually-steppable rAF mock, no synchronous-recursion trap);
      #   leaves envelope undefined when no speech was detected.

module: model_envelope_cache
  purpose: >
    WP-7a: schema for the offline-precomputed model-voice envelope numbers
    (build spec §5.2), plus the client's batch fetch/cache for them. The
    pipeline job that populates the table (decode mastered mp3 -> PCM -> same
    algorithm/constants -> upsert) lives in the dashboard repo as its own
    brief (WP-7b) — out of scope here.

  schema: >
    supabase/migrations/20260714_course_audio_envelope.sql (GATED — for Tom
    to apply, never ad-hoc, same rule as WP-4's persistence migration).
    course_audio_envelope: audio_id uuid PK (references course_audio.id),
    duration_ms, peak_count, peak_to_mean_ratio, mean_peak_width_ms,
    extractor_version int default 1, created_at. RLS on; anon + authenticated
    SELECT true (same posture as course_audio — read-only content data);
    writes are service-role only (the pipeline job). Ends with
    NOTIFY pgrst, 'reload schema'.

  data:
    ModelEnvelopeRow: { audioId, durationMs, peakCount, peakToMeanRatio, meanPeakWidthMs, extractorVersion }

  api:
    createEnvelopeMetadataCache(client: SupabaseClient) -> EnvelopeMetadataCache:
      >  One in-memory cache per session — deliberately simpler than
         listeningMetaCache's IndexedDB pattern, because stage 2 only ever
         runs with a live microphone (no mic -> no envelope evidence at all,
         so there is no offline case to serve).
    EnvelopeMetadataCache.fetchBatch(audioIds: string[]) -> Promise<void>:
      >  Chunks under the 150-id PostgREST in()-list cap (mirrors
         listeningMetaCache). Confirmed-missing ids cache as null so a repeat
         lookup this session doesn't re-fetch; a fetch failure leaves ids
         uncached (undefined) so a later call retries — never poisons a
         transient failure as a permanent null.
    EnvelopeMetadataCache.get(audioId) -> ModelEnvelopeRow | null | undefined:
      >  undefined = never fetched; null = fetched, confirmed no row yet.

  guarantees:
    - missing_row_no_op: a course with no envelope rows yet degrades to
      "stage 2 produces nothing for those cycles", never an error
    - no_stale_poisoning: fetch failures are retryable, confirmed absence is not

  tests:
    - packages/player-vue/src/composables/useEnvelopeMetadataCache.test.ts
      # fetch + camelCase mapping; confirmed-missing -> null; never-fetched ->
      # undefined; cache hit avoids re-fetch; fetch failure leaves undefined
      # for retry; chunking a 320-id list into 150/150/20.

module: envelope_delta_producer
  purpose: >
    Producer #3 on the evidence wire (build spec §5.3, WP-8). Per cycle with
    both a learner envelope capture and a model envelope row present,
    computes the learner-vs-model delta vector and emits one
    MasteryEvidence(source:'envelope') — the same wire the WP-1 behavioural
    producer feeds. Per-LEGO cross-phrase correlation (owner decision C, the
    second-differential fitness function) falls out of the aggregator for
    free: every phrase sharing a LEGO emits to the same unitId, so the merged
    series IS the cross-phrase delta series, and the downstream B4 curvature
    read on it IS the second differential — this producer's only job is one
    faithful per-cycle delta, not the differencing itself.

  delta_formula: >
    d_dur   = |learner.durationMs - model.durationMs| / model.durationMs
    d_peaks = |learner.peakCount - model.peakCount| / max(model.peakCount, 1)
    d_shape = |log(learner.peakToMeanRatio / model.peakToMeanRatio)|
            + |log(learner.meanPeakWidthMs / model.meanPeakWidthMs)|
    value   = w_dur*d_dur + w_peaks*d_peaks + w_shape*d_shape
    PROPOSED weights (config-tunable later, same as WP-1's mapping table):
      duration 0.5, peaks 0.3, shape 0.2 — duration carries the most fluency
      signal per the paper's 2.5x-length example. Producer confidence for
      every emitted event: weight 0.8 (PROPOSED).
    Zero-peak degenerate case (a silent/undetected side has peakToMeanRatio/
    meanPeakWidthMs of 0): each log-ratio term guards to 0 rather than
    +-Infinity/NaN when either operand isn't a positive finite number — the
    spec doesn't address this directly; "no shape signal from this term"
    beats letting one degenerate side swamp the whole delta.

  no_op_conditions: >
    - no learner envelope, or the capture-quality gate discarded it (weight 0)
    - no model row yet for this audio id (course without envelope data; cache
      miss, confirmed-null or not-yet-fetched both no-op identically)
    - extractor_version mismatch between learner and model — the two sides
      used different pinned constants, so the numbers aren't comparable;
      skip rather than compare incomparable numbers

  api:
    computeEnvelopeDelta(learner: EnvelopeMetadata, model: ModelEnvelopeRow,
                          weights?) -> { value, dDur, dPeaks, dShape }:
      >  Pure delta math, independently testable against the exact formula.
    recordEnvelopeEvidence(args: { sink, cache, legoId, audioId,
                                   learnerEnvelope, cycleId?, occurredAtMs,
                                   weights? }) -> MasteryEvidence | null:
      >  Computes the delta (when both sides are usable) and calls
         sink.record(); returns the emitted evidence or null on any no-op
         condition above. Holds only the EvidenceSink interface, same as
         WP-1's useBehaviouralEvidence — has no opinion on where the evidence
         ends up.

  wiring_status: >
    NOT YET CALLED from the cycle-complete path. useAdaptationEngine.ts and
    LearningPlayer.vue are a concurrent worker's files (WP-3: player wiring)
    — this module is fully built and tested but deliberately left
    unregistered, with a one-line TODO comment at the bottom of
    useEnvelopeEvidence.ts marking the registration point WP-3 needs to wire
    (call recordEnvelopeEvidence beside recordCycle, once WP-3 exposes the
    shared aggregator as an EvidenceSink and calls
    EnvelopeMetadataCache.fetchBatch with the round's target1 audio ids).

  guarantees:
    - pure_delta_math: computeEnvelopeDelta has no side effects, independently
      testable against the exact §5.3 formula
    - graceful_absence: every no-op condition (no capture, no model row,
      version mismatch) returns null and never throws
    - no_numeric_contamination: the zero-peak guard keeps a degenerate side
      from producing Infinity/NaN in the emitted evidence value

  tests:
    - packages/player-vue/src/composables/useEnvelopeEvidence.test.ts
      # computeEnvelopeDelta: zero delta on identical envelopes; the paper's
      #   2.5x-duration example; d_peaks/d_shape formula checks; zero-peak
      #   guard produces a finite, non-NaN value; custom weights honoured.
      # recordEnvelopeEvidence: emits one correctly-shaped MasteryEvidence
      #   when both sides are usable; no-ops on missing learner envelope,
      #   weight-0 capture, confirmed-missing model row, not-yet-fetched
      #   model row, and extractor_version mismatch — none of these throw.
